[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "ADR-2608122300"
  :adr/title "Close the repository-ownership migration around Etzhayyim and Kotobase"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-08-12"
  :adr/supersedes ""
  :adr/superseded-by ""
  :adr/body
  "## Context

The repository inventory had accumulated several different ownership concerns in the same GitHub organizations. Etzhayyim is Jun Kawasaki's personal project and Tamaki-centred artificial organism, while Cloud Itonami is an operational product plane, Kotoba Lang owns portable language/protocol substrate, AWAI Network owns the broader AWAI business plane, and Kotobase now has a dedicated product organization at `net-kotobase`.

Repository names are interpreted together with their organization. A destination organization can therefore remove a redundant source prefix without changing the semantic subject: for example, `network-awai/net-kotobase-engine` becomes `net-kotobase/engine`.

## Decision

### Etzhayyim boundary

`etzhayyim` remains the home of Tamaki, the artificial-organism actors, their organs, organism-specific applications, and Jun Kawasaki's personal Etzhayyim experiments. The remaining actor-like repositories are not renamed merely to normalize an `actor-` prefix, and repositories whose names no longer start with `com-etzhayyim-` are not subjected to another naming campaign.

Reusable language or protocol artifacts leave Etzhayyim for `kotoba-lang`; operational applications leave for `cloud-itonami`. This session applied that rule to:

- `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-open-wellbecoming` -> `kotoba-lang/open-wellbecoming`
- `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-app-society6` -> `cloud-itonami/app-society6`

The remaining `com-etzhayyim-*` actors and organism applications were reviewed and retained because their identity is specifically Tamaki/Etzhayyim rather than a shared library or a general business application.

The final live GitHub inventory at session closure contains 75 Etzhayyim repositories: 68 active and 7 archived. The 68 active repositories comprise 33 normalized `actor-*` repositories, 12 retained legacy-name actor repositories, 20 organism applications, and the three core/meta repositories `tamaki`, `root`, and `architecture-framework`.

The 12 retained legacy-name actors are `com-etzhayyim-abaki`, `com-etzhayyim-hibiki`, `com-etzhayyim-hirameki`, `com-etzhayyim-minori`, `com-etzhayyim-tawami`, `com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi`, `com-etzhayyim-torifune`, `com-etzhayyim-tsumugi`, `com-etzhayyim-umisachi`, `com-etzhayyim-wakai`, `com-etzhayyim-yoro`, and `com-etzhayyim-yudane`. The 20 retained applications are `com-etzhayyim-app-explorer`, `com-etzhayyim-app-hakkou`, `com-etzhayyim-app-kabi`, `com-etzhayyim-app-karma`, `com-etzhayyim-app-ki`, `com-etzhayyim-app-kinoko`, `com-etzhayyim-app-kiyome`, `com-etzhayyim-app-kobo`, `com-etzhayyim-app-koke`, `com-etzhayyim-app-mold-allergy`, `com-etzhayyim-app-omikuji`, `com-etzhayyim-app-open-ossekai`, `com-etzhayyim-app-organism`, `com-etzhayyim-app-organism-viz`, `com-etzhayyim-app-otakiage`, `com-etzhayyim-app-resources`, `com-etzhayyim-app-saikin`, `com-etzhayyim-app-seibutsu`, `com-etzhayyim-app-seigen-cue`, and `com-etzhayyim-app-shinka`.

These 32 legacy-prefixed active repositories are not migration gaps. No additional repository is currently approved or identified for transfer from Etzhayyim to `cloud-itonami` or `kotoba-lang`. The 7 archived repositories are historical retention and lifecycle-policy work, not ownership-migration backlog.

### Kotobase boundary

The externally operated Kotobase product/service plane belongs to `net-kotobase`. Portable Kotoba/Kotobase engine, storage, protocol, and client libraries remain in `kotoba-lang`. Broader AWAI company and operator repositories remain in `network-awai`.

This session established the following product-plane identities:

| Previous identity | Canonical identity |
| --- | --- |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase` | `net-kotobase/control-plane` |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase-ipfs` | `net-kotobase/ipfs` |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase-engine` | `net-kotobase/engine` |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase-authn` | `net-kotobase/authn` |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase-cypher` | `net-kotobase/cypher` |
| `network-awai/net-kotobase-lake` | `net-kotobase/lake` |
| `kotoba-lang/kotobase-docs` | `net-kotobase/docs` |
| `kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor` | `net-kotobase/commoncrawl-actor` |
| `kotoba-lang/net-kotobase-commoncrawler` | `net-kotobase/commoncrawler` |

The pre-existing `net-kotobase/sdk` remains unchanged. `authn` was an empty repository, so it had no reviewable source change before transfer; it was initialized on `main` after transfer. Other moved repositories carried a merged boundary README change through a pull request.

### Manifest and fleet closure

The root manifest now declares the `net-kotobase` remote, group, organization/domain vocabulary, project paths, relocations, and preserved repository identity where applicable. The generated `manifest/west.yml` and fleet-db projection were reconciled. Minimal `--entry` generation was also corrected to synchronize generated remote/group headers when a new organization is introduced.

## Evidence

- Etzhayyim moves landed in root PRs #2094 (`8f4066857141204259910ff3b1eaf9bddff9e932`) and #2096 (`f8fd5b6f89de16e2f513615c7098e5290fb2e38f`).
- The nine-repository Kotobase organization move landed in root PR #2100 (`08c943b06603e3aaa7bf48650e8067e3ce01a02f`).
- The final post-transfer control-plane pin advance landed in root PR #2101 (`a957eb96b1211d4b07d0bbcea3e2afc280c52771`), pinning `fabd8408eccbfd79958dea55eafd509ffae85383`.
- At closure, each of the nine moved Kotobase project pins matched its canonical GitHub repository tip, and fleet-db matched the west projection.
- A final live GitHub organization inventory reported 75 Etzhayyim repositories (68 active and 7 archived), with zero confirmed ownership-migration gaps.

This is repository, naming, manifest, and fleet-placement evidence. It is not evidence that every production route, deployment, credential, or external integration was exercised after transfer; those remain service-specific verification work.

## Consequences

New Tamaki-specific actors and organs default to `etzhayyim`. New general operational applications default to `cloud-itonami`. New portable language/protocol substrate defaults to `kotoba-lang`. New Kotobase-specific operated services default to `net-kotobase` and should not repeat the organization name in the repository slug.

GitHub redirects preserve old repository URLs, while west paths and canonical identities use the new organizations. No further broad rename or transfer campaign is implied by this ADR. This repository-ownership migration session is closed at the verified boundary above."}]
